      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `file_operations` struct has a field called `this_module` containing a pointer to the `.ko` that owns this vtable. When files using that vtable are open, the kernel takes a refcount on that module, which prevents its code from being unloaded in case someone tries unload said kernel module.\n\nIf this field is not set and the vtable is declared in a loadable kernel module, then the module could be unloaded, freeing both the vtable global variable and the code associated with all the functions.",
      "parentUuid": "11da8bb8_06c64b8c",
      "revId": "e1dd750a074a6dfb22eb5cc577a1645d17ac65e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
